    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1067">

                <pb facs="0798" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.63/173</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Special Representative Rodgers
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-07T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1916, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>125. Consul, Nogales, reports decree 56, dated May 18, signed by Calles, given to
                    press Saturday, provides all mining properties in State continuing idle more
                    than 30 days from date of decree subject seizure and operation by State.</p>
                <p>Refer your No. 84, May 23, 5 p.m., and request immediate issuance similar orders
                    this case.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
